{"book":{"id":"book-kidnapped-souls-national-indifference-and-the-battle-for-children-in-the-bohemian-lands-1900-194","slug":"kidnapped-souls-national-indifference-and-the-battle-for-children-in-the-bohemian-lands-1900-194","title":"Kidnapped Souls: National Indifference and the Battle for Children in the Bohemian Lands 1900-1948","authors":[{"id":"person-tara-zahra","name":"Tara Zahra"}],"publisherId":"publisher-cornell-university-press","imprintId":"imprint-cornell-university-press","isbn13":["9780801461910"],"subjects":["History"],"topics":["Class, Poverty & Inequality","Nationalism & Authoritarianism","War & Military Strategy","Europe & Russia"],"centralFigures":[],"links":{"amazon":"https://www.amazon.com/s?k=Kidnapped%20Souls%3A%20National%20Indifference%20and%20the%20Battle%20for%20Children%20in%20the%20Bohemian%20Lands%201900-1948%20Tara%20Zahra","bookshop":"https://bookshop.org/search?keywords=Kidnapped%20Souls%3A%20National%20Indifference%20and%20the%20Battle%20for%20Children%20in%20the%20Bohemian%20Lands%201900-1948%20Tara%20Zahra","indiebound":"https://www.indiebound.org/search/book?keys=Kidnapped%20Souls%3A%20National%20Indifference%20and%20the%20Battle%20for%20Children%20in%20the%20Bohemian%20Lands%201900-1948%20Tara%20Zahra","worldcat":"https://search.worldcat.org/search?q=Kidnapped%20Souls%3A%20National%20Indifference%20and%20the%20Battle%20for%20Children%20in%20the%20Bohemian%20Lands%201900-1948%20Tara%20Zahra","publisher":"https://books.google.com/books/about/Kidnapped_Souls.html?hl=&id=OP16DwAAQBAJ"},"sourceIds":["source-award-record-laura-shannon-european-studies-laura-shannon-prize-2011-official-winner-page","source-google-books-kidnapped-souls-national-indifference-and-the-battle-for-children-in-the-bohemian-lands-1900-194","source-open-library-kidnapped-souls-national-indifference-and-the-battle-for-children-in-the-bohemian-lands-1900-194","source-cover-open-library-kidnapped-souls-national-indifference-and-the-battle-for-children-in-the-bohemian-lands-1900-194","source-imprint-normalization"],"subjectCategories":[{"source":"google_books","scheme":"google_books_category","label":"History","sourceId":"source-google-books-kidnapped-souls-national-indifference-and-the-battle-for-children-in-the-bohemian-lands-1900-194"}],"publicationYear":2011,"pageCount":300,"summary":"Throughout the nineteenth and into the early decades of the twentieth century, it was common for rural and working-class parents in the Czech-German borderlands to ensure that their children were bilingual by sending them to live with families who spoke the \"other\" language. As nationalism became a more potent force in Central Europe, however, such practices troubled pro-German and pro-Czech activists, who feared that the children born to their nation could literally be \"lost\" or \"kidnapped\" from the national community through such experiences and, more generally, by parents who were either flexible about national belonging or altogether indifferent to it. Highlighting this indifference to nationalism—and concerns about such apathy among nationalists—Kidnapped Souls offers a surprising new perspective on Central European politics and society in the first half of the twentieth century.","thumbnailUrl":"/book-covers/book-kidnapped-souls-national-indifference-and-the-battle-for-children-in-the-bohemian-lands-1900-194.jpg","readerProfile":{"readerLevel":"crossover","narrativeScore":0,"accessibilityScore":0,"scholarlyScore":0.356,"traits":[{"id":"academic","score":0.38,"confidence":"low","evidence":["academic press signal: Cornell University Press / Cornell University Press"]},{"id":"scholarly","score":0.28,"confidence":"low","evidence":["academic press signal: Cornell University Press / Cornell University Press"]}],"method":"deterministic_catalog_heuristics_v1"},"experimentalSemanticProfile":{"centralFigures":[],"centralPlaces":[],"argument":{"present":true,"statement":"As nationalism intensified in Central Europe, activists reframed paren